abstract: >-
  OpenGenesis-BioCore is a local-first, extensible bioinformatics platform
  designed for reproducible analysis workflows on Windows and Linux. Version
  0.5.0 builds on the canonical small-variant and Workflow Engine 2.0 layers
  with a Project & Sample Workspace: revision-controlled research metadata,
  sample registry and input/reference binding, deterministic batch planning and
  execution, explicit resume/retry attempt lineage, lineage-aware QC/results,
  integrity-verified result manifests and HTML reports, and an integrated local
  browser workspace. The release retains the C++20 native core, localhost-only
  browser interface, SQLite persistence, native plugins, exact-version workflow
  templates, scientific benchmark gates, and local-first provenance model.

